    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d260">

                <pb facs="0507" n="497" sameAs="frus:frus1946v10/pg497"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by General Marshall to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">OSE 569</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-11-09">9 November
                        1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Recently I called upon the U. S. Commissioner at Peiping<anchor n="94"
                        xml:id="d260-f1"/> to give me his estimate of the extent to which the
                    effectiveness of teams and Executive Headquarters had been limited by the ill
                    will and suspicion generated by Communist propaganda.</p>
                <p>Attached is a paraphrased message and his report<anchor n="95" xml:id="d260-f2"/>
                    on this subject.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>G. C. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d260-a1.xml" xpointer="d260-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d260-f1" n="94" xml:id="d260-f1-content">
                <p>Lt. Gen. Alvan C. Gillem, Jr.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d260-f2" n="95" xml:id="d260-f2-content">
